From d5b692ee0b6cba8ea5dc4677c6f2ff2d74ce566e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr233 <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 04:26:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 69/70] vgpu: answer heap texture queries for a task still
 queued on a child ring

Component: runtime drain, heap texture size/align replies (all pathways).

A heap texture size query can name a task whose DEFINE_TASK2 is still
sitting on a child ring behind a held packet, which happens on 27.2 while
channel 1 waits for a translation. The reply path looked the task up in the
active table only, found nothing and declined (cmd_task_dead), so the guest
got no size for that texture.

reply_fence::find is now a wrapper over a generic scan, and a new
reply_fence::queued lists the matching records on a ring.
reply_heap_texture_size_and_align still answers through the active task when
there is one. Otherwise it looks for the last queued DEFINE_TASK2 for that task
id on child rings 1..MAX_CHANNELS, installs its entry for the length of the
reply, then puts back whatever was there before. Each answer is logged as
heap_texture_query queued_task.

Verified:
- cargo test -p reims-vgpu --no-default-features
  --features backend-vulkan,host-window -- --test-threads=1: 2344 lib tests
  and every integration test pass (llvm-dis on PATH).
- clippy -D warnings on the same arm reports 65 diagnostics with and
  without this change on rustc 1.99.1. All of them predate it (new lints
  such as chunks_exact_to_as_chunks).
- Live on arm64 Linux (NVIDIA GB10), macOS 27.2 guest: the queued_task
  line appears and the queries it covers are answered.

Not verified: the backend-metal and x86 clippy arms, and any visible change
that can be put down to this commit alone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
